-- Declared `Time64(9)` typed path keeps all nine fractional digits
00:00:00.123456789	Time64(9)
{"t":"00:00:00.123456789"}
-- The same file read back as plain JSON exposes the residual decimal
{"t":0.123456789}	{'t':'Decimal(18, 9)'}
-- Declared `Time64(7)` typed path
12:34:56.1234567	Time64(7)
-- `Time64(6)` still uses the `TIME(MICROS)` primitive
12:34:56.123456	Time64(6)
{"t":"12:34:56.123456"}	{'t':'Time64(6)'}
-- `Dynamic` values: mixed types force the residual path; nothing is truncated
86399.999999999	Decimal(18, 9)
-0.000000001	Decimal(18, 9)
00:00:01.500000	Time64(6)
x	String
